  It's a plain HTML checkbox, so the browser handles checking and unchecking with no JavaScript. Because it's wrapped in
  a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, clicking the word "Done" toggles it too. I haven't opened the page in a browser to check it.

  The page doesn't have a task list yet, so this is a single checkbox labelled "Done". When you add task items, you can
  put one of these next to each item. Also, the checked state resets when the page reloads. If you want it to persist,
  that would need a small script, for example one that saves to [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m.

